Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Verified: pendingDeletePaths is written in pinForEdit /
pinForMediaRemoval but a whole-tree grep finds no read anywhere, so a
delete requested through a path that never went through Layer 1 (the
process died between the pin insert and the Layer-1 record in the same
storage pass) was never deleted after the copy terminated. Fix: in
startupReconcile, for each PINNED/COPYING ref with a non-empty
pendingDeletePaths, INSERT OR IGNORE one DeferredDelete row per path
(size/mtime from the ref — statted at record time when 0,0 per D-04 —
requestedBy EDIT_TAIL, cancelDeferred from the ref). Placement is
deliberately BEFORE step 4 rather than step 5 as the audit suggests:
step 4's terminal transitions (GATE_OFF / UNAVAILABLE / FAILED, incl.
the D-11 change) release the synthesised rows through their normal
release calls; rows for pins that stay active are skipped by the
release's active-pin re-check and release when the pin terminates.
A row Layer 1 already recorded is not duplicated (unique index).
---
 .../ayugram/aligram/AliGramPreservation.java  | 38 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 38 insertions(+)

diff --git a/TMessagesProj/src/main/java/com/radolyn/ayugram/aligram/AliGramPreservation.java b/TMessagesProj/src/main/java/com/radolyn/ayugram/aligram/AliGramPreservation.java
index 72b4074a2..5e5176242 100644
--- a/TMessagesProj/src/main/java/com/radolyn/ayugram/aligram/AliGramPreservation.java
+++ b/TMessagesProj/src/main/java/com/radolyn/ayugram/aligram/AliGramPreservation.java
@@ -2647,6 +2647,44 @@ public final class AliGramPreservation {
         } catch (Throwable e) {
             FileLog.e(TAG + ": fakeId verification failed", e);
         }
+        // D-12 synthesis (BEFORE step 4, deliberately — not in step 5 as
+        // the audit suggests its placement): pendingDeletePaths is the
+        // crash-recovery seed, written at pin time but never read — if
+        // the process died between the pin insert and the Layer-1 record
+        // in the same storage pass, no DeferredDelete row exists for the
+        // file. Synthesise one per recorded path (INSERT OR IGNORE: a
+        // row Layer-1 already recorded is not duplicated; the size/mtime
+        // come from the ref, or are statted at record time when 0,0).
+        // It runs before step 4 so that step 4's terminal transitions
+        // (GATE_OFF / UNAVAILABLE / FAILED) release the synthesised rows
+        // through their normal release calls; rows for pins that stay
+        // active are skipped by the release's active-pin re-check and
+        // release when the pin terminates. Cancel intent comes from the
+        // pin (cancelDeferred) for the same reason.
+        try {
+            for (PreservedRef ref : dao.getNonTerminalRefs()) {
+                if (ref.accountId != account) {
+                    continue;
+                }
+                if (!AliGramEligibility.STATE_PINNED.equals(ref.state)
+                        && !AliGramEligibility.STATE_COPYING.equals(ref.state)) {
+                    continue;
+                }
+                if (ref.pendingDeletePaths == null || ref.pendingDeletePaths.isEmpty()) {
+                    continue;
+                }
+                for (String rawPath : ref.pendingDeletePaths.split(",")) {
+                    String path = rawPath == null ? "" : rawPath.trim();
+                    if (path.isEmpty()) {
+                        continue;
+                    }
+                    recordDeferredDelete(account, ref.refId, path, ref.sourceSize, ref.sourceMtime,
+                            "EDIT_TAIL", ref.cancelDeferred);
+                }
+            }
+        } catch (Throwable e) {
+            FileLog.e(TAG + ": deferred-delete synthesis failed", e);
+        }
         // 4. Reset DOWNLOADING/COPYING → ENQUEUED after gate re-check;
         //    re-drive PINNED rows whose source is on disk; PINNED rows
         //    with no source go straight to UNAVAILABLE (D-11 — they can
